    "malware_behavior": "**1. Summary (2\u20113 sentences)**  \nThe sample is a Windows\u2011executable that runs silently on the host, gathers basic system information (such as OS version, hostname, and user account details), and writes that data to a hidden file in the user\u2019s profile. It does not attempt any network communication, so its primary purpose appears to be local reconnaissance and data collection for later use by an attacker who may retrieve the file through another vector.\n\n**2. Technical Details (how it works)**  \n\n| Step | What the malware does | How it is implemented |\n|------|-----------------------|-----------------------|\n| **Execution & Persistence** | The binary is launched either manually or via a dropper. It creates a hidden folder (e.g., `%APPDATA%\\{random}`) and drops a hidden file (`data.bin`) to store collected information. | Uses standard WinAPI calls such as `CreateDirectoryW`, `SetFileAttributesW` (FILE_ATTRIBUTE_HIDDEN), and `CreateFileW` with `FILE_ATTRIBUTE_HIDDEN | FILE_ATTRIBUTE_SYSTEM`. |\n| **Privilege Check** | Determines whether it is running with administrative rights. | Calls `OpenProcessToken` and `GetTokenInformation` to query `TokenElevation`. |\n| **System Information Gathering** | Collects: <br>\u2022 OS version and build number <br>\u2022 Computer name and domain <br>\u2022 Logged\u2011on user name and SID <br>\u2022 List of installed hotfixes <br>\u2022 Processor architecture and amount of RAM | Uses a mix of WinAPI functions (`GetVersionExW`, `GetComputerNameW`, `GetUserNameW`, `LookupAccountSidW`, `RegOpenKeyExW` for HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall, `GlobalMemoryStatusEx`). |\n| **File System Enumeration** | Scans the user\u2019s profile directory for certain file types (e.g., `.docx`, `.pdf`) and records their paths",
